    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW22f6Y1Nv4WY5KWBa3A7g69G)_\n\n**Before:** six theme packages declared in `sp-themes.el`, `sp-load-theme` only wraps `load-theme`, and several modules (`sp-macos`, the dashboards, `toggle-dark-light-theme`) pick themes on their own.\n\n**After:** `docs/architecture/theme-system-design.org`, documentation only:\n- Comparison of modus, ef, doric, lambda and catppuccin: palette structure, options, faces covered, extension mechanisms, hooks, licences and what vendoring costs (Ef requires the Modus engine).\n- Ten features ranked for adoption (registry with metadata, two-layer palette overrides, `with-colors`, face bundles, tiny theme files, …).\n- Proposed layout for `libraries/themes/` and `sp-load-theme` as the single entry point, in five separable steps, plus three open questions.\n- Found while reading: `modus-themes-prompts` and `-completions` are obsolete since 5.3.0 and `modus-themes-org-blocks` no longer exists, so those settings in `sp-themes.el` do nothing today.\n\n**Checked:** facts come from the upstream sources cloned at their current `main`. **Not checked:** nothing was run in Emacs; no code changed.\n\nCHANGELOG: new set \"Themes\" under Open pull requests.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_013wuoefeVHQQNwZgJptsdeH)_",
